# Force LF for files whose bytes are hashed or executed as scripts, so behavior is identical
# regardless of the checking-out OS/git config. Without this, a Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true)
# and a Linux CI runner can end up with different line endings for the "same" file, which would
# break MigrationImmutabilityTest's checksums (KH-0.2.2) and shell script shebangs.
*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
